---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GoalSelector from '../components/guide/GoalSelector.astro';
import LeaderboardWalkthrough from '../components/guide/LeaderboardWalkthrough.astro';
import StatusInterpreter from '../components/guide/StatusInterpreter.astro';
import ModelComparison from '../components/guide/ModelComparison.astro';
import AnalysisMap from '../components/guide/AnalysisMap.astro';
import EvaluationWorksheet from '../components/guide/EvaluationWorksheet.astro';
import { guideCapacity } from '../data/guide';
import { PRICING_CHECKED_ON } from '../data/modelPricing';
import { articles } from '../data/articles';
import '../styles/guide.css';
const weights = guideCapacity[0]?.levels.map(level=>level.weight) ?? [];
const formatDate=(date:string)=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{dateStyle:'long',timeZone:'UTC'}).format(new Date(`${date}T00:00:00Z`));
---
<Layout title="How to Use Ultimate Bench | Practical Guide" description="Learn how to read Ultimate Bench scores, compare AI model configurations, understand coverage and statuses, use Analysis, account for price, and run a private evaluation.">
<main class="guide-page">
 <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Practical decision guide</p><h1>Use Ultimate Bench<br /><span>without overreading it.</span></h1><p>Learn what to inspect, which score matters for your decision, how to compare configurations fairly, and when this benchmark cannot answer your question.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary" href="#goals">Start with my goal</a><a href="/#global-leaderboard">View leaderboard</a><a href="/analysis">Explore Analysis</a><a href="/methodology">Read Methodology</a></div></header>
 <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>On this page</strong><a href="#goals">Choose a path</a><a href="#leaderboard">Read results</a><a href="#scores">Choose a score</a><a href="#statuses">Interpret status</a><a href="#compare">Compare</a><a href="#evaluate">Test privately</a></nav>
 <GoalSelector />
 <LeaderboardWalkthrough />
 <section id="scores" class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="scores-title"><p class="step">03 · Choose the evidence</p><h2 id="scores-title">Use the score that matches your question.</h2><div class="decision-flow"><article><strong>Specific capability</strong><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><p><b>Arena score.</b> Visual localization or spatial binding → Visual Bench. Difficult evidence retrieval and source synthesis → DATA Bench. Chess-position analysis or play → Chess Bench.</p></article><article><strong>Broad three-arena comparison</strong><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><p><b>Overall.</b> The equal mean of canonical arena scores for globally qualified configurations. It is not a universal intelligence score and can hide specialization.</p></article><article><strong>Reliability or failure threshold</strong><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><p><b>Level results + Analysis.</b> Similar aggregates can conceal steady performance, late collapse, invalid output, or strength concentrated in a heavily weighted level.</p></article><article><strong>Deployment decision</strong><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><p><b>Shortlist + private evaluation.</b> Public evidence cannot verify your prompts, constraints, users, or failure costs.</p></article></div>
 <div class="denominator"><div><p class="step">Why percentages look low</p><h3>Arena scores are weighted shares of permanent capacity—not simply “questions correct.”</h3><p>Each arena reserves six level positions with progressive weights {weights.join(', ')}. Planned or Locked capacity remains in the denominator, so the maximum currently earnable score can be below 100%. Percent signs from unrelated benchmarks do not make their values comparable.</p></div><div class="capacity-grid">{guideCapacity.map(item=><article><h4>{item.name}</h4><dl><div><dt>Permanent denominator</dt><dd>{item.denominator}</dd></div><div><dt>Active operational weight</dt><dd>{item.operational}</dd></div><div><dt>Reserved weight</dt><dd>{item.reserved}</dd></div><div><dt>Current maximum</dt><dd>{item.maximum.toFixed(2)}%</dd></div></dl></article>)}</div><p class="worked"><strong>Plain-language example:</strong> if a configuration earned 100 at the first two Active levels and zero elsewhere, it earns <code>(100×{weights[0]} + 100×{weights[1]}) ÷ {guideCapacity[0].denominator} = {((100*(weights[0]+weights[1]))/guideCapacity[0].denominator).toFixed(2)}%</code>. The unused and reserved higher-level weight stays in the denominator.</p><a href="/methodology#scoring">Read the formal scoring method →</a></div>
 </section>
 <StatusInterpreter /><ModelComparison /><AnalysisMap />
 <section id="price" class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="price-title"><p class="step">07 · Practical fit</p><h2 id="price-title">Capability and suitability are different questions.</h2><p>Ultimate Bench keeps canonical results untouched by price. Its separate cost view uses maintained API list prices checked <strong>{formatDate(PRICING_CHECKED_ON)}</strong> and an explicit blend of 75% input price plus 25% output price, per one million tokens. Missing verified pricing is shown as unavailable, never estimated.</p><p>That blend is only an orientation assumption. Caching, batches, retries, tool calls, failures, and your input/output mix change operating cost; consumer subscriptions and API prices may not be comparable.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Quality on the relevant work</li><li>Total cost, including review and reruns</li><li>Speed and throughput</li><li>Actual availability</li><li>Required tool access</li><li>Context constraints</li><li>Privacy and data handling</li><li>Consequences of failure</li></ul><p class="links"><a href="/#pareto-title">Open the separate price view</a><a href="/blog/cost-adjusted-ai-scores">Read the visible-formula article</a></p></section>
 <section id="recipes" class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="recipes-title"><p class="step">08 · Decision recipes</p><h2 id="recipes-title">Follow a workflow—not a universal recommendation.</h2><div class="recipes"><details open><summary>“I want the strongest general result”</summary><p>Start with qualified Overall → inspect arena profile and coverage → use Analysis trade-offs and Pareto status → compare constraints → run a private evaluation.</p></details><details><summary>“I mainly need difficult information retrieval”</summary><p>Prioritize DATA Bench → inspect its level results → open failure anatomy → check source-related limitations → do not let unrelated Chess performance dominate.</p></details><details><summary>“Two configurations have almost the same score”</summary><p>Treat them as a neighborhood → remember rank uses full precision while display is rounded → compare arena and level shapes → compare access and cost → test both privately.</p></details><details><summary>“A cheaper model looks surprisingly competitive”</summary><p>Verify the same pricing basis → inspect sacrificed capabilities → estimate your workload → include review, retry, and failure costs.</p></details><details><summary>“The top result is unavailable to me”</summary><p>Filter to configurations you can actually access. Availability is a deployment constraint, not a theoretical model property.</p></details><details><summary>“My task is not tested here”</summary><p>Use Ultimate Bench only as background evidence. Create a private target-task evaluation and do not extrapolate arena ranks into unrelated capabilities.</p></details></div></section>
 <EvaluationWorksheet />
 <section id="mistakes" class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="mistakes-title"><p class="step">10 · Interpretation guardrails</p><h2 id="mistakes-title">Do not make these mistakes.</h2><div class="mistakes">{[['Treat Overall as universal intelligence','Match an arena to the task, or test the unmeasured task privately.'],['Compare unrelated percentages','Read each denominator and scoring construct first.'],['Ignore PROVISIONAL','Check coverage and official rank eligibility.'],['Treat INVALID as a numeric zero','Preserve the distinct event even though both contribute zero points.'],['Use only the provider name','Compare the exact tested model, tools, and reasoning configuration.'],['Use release date as evaluation date','Treat it only as model-release metadata.'],['Call a decimal gap decisive','Treat close results as a neighborhood without uncertainty evidence.'],['Ignore level failure shape','Open level results and Analysis failure anatomy.'],['Equate low list price with low total cost','Include calls, retries, review, and failure consequences.'],['Extrapolate into untested tasks','Run representative private cases.'],['Choose without real-work testing','Use the downloadable worksheet.'],['Assume Analysis proves causation','Read patterns as associations and paired observations.']].map(([bad,better])=><article><h3>{bad}</h3><p><strong>Instead:</strong> {better}</p></article>)}</div></section>
 <section id="map" class="guide-section site-map" aria-labelledby="map-title"><p class="step">11 · Where next?</p><h2 id="map-title">Use each part of the site for one job.</h2><div>{[['/','Leaderboard','Published ranks, scores, coverage, level results, and practical views.'],['/analysis','Analysis','Transfer, failures, matched configurations, trade-offs, and sensitivity.'],['/methodology','Methodology','Administration, scoring, qualification, status rules, and limitations.'],['/guide','Guide','What to inspect and how to combine the evidence.'],['/blog','Articles','Longer editorial explanations and benchmark-literacy field notes.']].map(([href,title,text])=><a href={href}><strong>{title}</strong><span>{text}</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></a>)}</div></section>
 <section id="reading" class="guide-section further" aria-labelledby="reading-title"><p class="step">12 · Further reading</p><h2 id="reading-title">Field notes for a deeper read.</h2><div>{articles.map(article=><article><p>{article.readingTime}</p><h3><a href={`/blog/${article.slug}`}>{article.title}</a></h3><span>{article.description}</span></article>)}</div><a class="archive" href="/blog">Browse all Articles →</a></section>
</main></Layout>
